[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:In or Out?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.22]Why did Rex run away? | 为什么雷克斯跑掉了？
[00:15.52]Our dog, Rex, used to sit outside our front gate and bark. | 我们的狗雷克斯过去常蹲在大门外吠叫。
[00:22.54]Every time he wanted to come into the garden he would bark until someone opened the gate. | 每当它想进花园时就会吠叫，直到有人开门才罢休。
[00:30.39]As the neighbours complained of the noise, my husband spent weeks training him to press his paw on the latch to let himself in. | 由于邻居们抱怨狗叫声，我丈夫花了几个星期训练它用爪子按门闩，好自己进来。
[00:41.56]Rex soon became an expert at opening the gate. | 雷克斯很快成了开门的行家。
[00:46.22]However, when I was going out shopping last week, I noticed him in the garden near the gate. | 然而，上星期当我外出购物时，发现它正待在花园大门附近。
[00:54.81]This time he was barking so that someone would let him out! | 这次它吠叫是想要人放它出去！
[01:00.09]Since then, he has developed another bad habit. | 从那以后，它又养成了一个坏习惯。
[01:05.10]As soon as he opens the gate from the outside, he comes into the garden and waits until the gate shuts. | 它从外边把门打开后，就进花园等着门关上。
[01:14.07]Then he sits and barks until someone lets him out. | 然后就蹲着叫，直到有人放它出去。
[01:18.58]After this he immediately lets himself in and begins barking again. | 这之后它立刻又自己进来，接着又开始叫。
[01:26.28]Yesterday my husband removed the gate and Rex got so annoyed we have not seen him since. | 昨天我丈夫把大门拆了，雷克斯非常恼火，此后我们就再没见到过它。
